## Run PromQL queries against Elasticsearch

PromQL (GA) now covers about 92% of the queries used in the top 100 Grafana dashboards, up from 43.4% in Elasticsearch 9.4. The additions include vector matching and `label_join`, `label_replace`, as well as functions such as `topk`. You can point existing dashboards at Elasticsearch without rewriting queries, and an automated A/B test against native Prometheus checks that results match. Learn how we built PromQL into Elasticsearch.

## Multiuser chat in Kibana

Kibana chats now support multiple users in the same conversation (in technical preview). Access can be set three ways: public to all users, restricted to specific users in an organization, or private. Your Elasticsearch agents can now work with your whole team in the same conversation. Any participant in the chat can prompt the agent, and all the users in the conversation see the response. Read more in the deep dive blog.

